# 04 Security Privacy

## Goal
Apply privacy-by-default and baseline security for auth, rewards, and player data.

## Always
- Store only minimum required data.
- Keep secrets out of the repository.
- Model auth and identity flows explicitly.
- Validate reward and leaderboard mutations server-side.
- Keep analytics free of unnecessary personal data.

## Trust boundaries
- Client may propose actions.
- Server validates economy-relevant writes.
- Security-sensitive decisions must not trust client input alone.

## Prohibited
- Hardcoded API keys or secrets.
- PII in logs or analytics events without strict necessity and approval.
- Client-side trust for token, lives, XP, or leaderboard updates.
